    "n": 42,
    "title": "PostgreSQL transaction succeeds after a caught statement error",
    "state": "open",
    "author": "dev-ahn",
    "assignees": [
      "cora"
    ],
    "labels": [
      "bug",
      "sql"
    ],
    "opened": "2026-10-15T04:20:00Z",
    "updated": "2026-10-18T03:20:00Z",
    "body": "A PostgreSQL statement error can be caught inside `withTransaction`. PostgreSQL then responds to `COMMIT` with `ROLLBACK`, but the effect reports success.\n\n```ts\nyield* sql.withTransaction(\n  sql`SELECT missing_column FROM example`.pipe(Effect.catch(() => Effect.void))\n)\n```\n\nExpected: the transaction fails and the next query can borrow a clean connection.",
    "comments": [
      {
        "author": "cora",
        "date": "2026-10-15T22:20:00Z",
        "body": "Confirmed with a caught PostgreSQL statement error. I made a TODO for the driver and shared transaction contract."
      },
      {
        "author": "smithers-agent",
        "date": "2026-10-18T02:20:00Z",
        "body": "The PR checks the PostgreSQL command tag and adds a driver commit hook. The shared SQL change also reaches the Bun SQLite tests.",
        "agent": {
          "run": "run-4801",
          "flow": "implement-issue",
          "harness": "Codex · gpt-6.1-sol",
          "for": "cora"
        }
      },
      {
        "author": "maya",
        "date": "2026-10-18T03:20:00Z",
        "body": "The PostgreSQL regression is covered. Fix the Bun rollback failure before I can merge."
      }
    ],
